{"hits": {"hits": [{"created": "2024-07-06T01:36:48.551312+00:00", "modified": "2024-07-08T14:34:44.950204+00:00", "id": 12667738, "conceptrecid": "12664229", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.12667738", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.12664229", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.12667738", "metadata": {"title": "ISSTA'24 Artifact - Prospector: Boosting Directed Grey-box Fuzzing for Large-scale Target Sets with Iterative Prioritization", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.12667738", "publication_date": "2024-07-06", "description": "<h1>README</h1>\n<p>In the Prospector-artifact v2, we upload the &nbsp;\"RQ1_crashes_all.tar.gz\", containing all the seeds generated by all fuzzers. These seeds are used to calculate TTR and TTE for RQ1. Since \"RQ1_crashes_all.tar.gz\" is too large and requires a significant amount of time to analyze, we provide the results of the analyzed crashes in Prospector-artifact v1. Therefore, the decision to download \"RQ1_crashes_all.tar.gz\" can be made based on individual needs.</p>\n<h2>Acknowledge</h2>\n<p>We greatly appreciate the artifacts from <a href=\"https://github.com/HexHive/FishFuzz\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">FishFuzz</a> and <a href=\"https://github.com/prosyslab/DAFL-artifact\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">DAFL</a>. The Prospector-artifact has benefited significantly from these two works.</p>\n<h2>Contact</h2>\n<p>If you have any questions &amp; find any bugs, feel free to contact me via <a href=\"mailto:iskindar97@gmail.com\">iskindar97@gmail.com</a>.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Zhang, Zhijie", "affiliation": "Institute of Information Engineering", "orcid": "0000-0001-9751-8268"}], "resource_type": {"title": "Conference paper", "type": "publication", "subtype": "conferencepaper"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 1, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "12664229"}}]}}, "title": "ISSTA'24 Artifact - Prospector: Boosting Directed Grey-box Fuzzing